From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: do not dereference an unpopulated role in cdns_role_stop()

The role switch is registered in cdns_init() before cdns_core_init_role()
fills cdns->roles[]. On CIX Sky1 boards the rts5453 USB-PD controller can
call usb_role_switch_set_role() in that window, and cdns_role_stop() then
dereferences cdns->roles[role], which is still NULL (oops at offset 0x28,
the ->state member).

Return early when the role driver is not registered yet.

Tested on an Orange Pi 6 Plus (CIX CD8180) with 6.18.14 and the Sky1
series.

Signed-off-by: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/core.c
@@ -59,6 +59,10 @@ static void cdns_role_stop(struct cdns *cdns)
 	if (WARN_ON(role > USB_ROLE_DEVICE))
 		return;
 
+	/* roles[] is populated after the role switch is registered */
+	if (!cdns->roles[role])
+		return;
+
 	if (cdns->roles[role]->state == CDNS_ROLE_STATE_INACTIVE)
 		return;
 
